Jodes the Lady made a good run, but came a up short.  It's sad to say that
this was an unnecessary and stupid death (aren't they all ;-)), but its
happy in that many lessons were learned.

If you don't want to read about Jodes' two-week journey or see some
possible spolers, hit 'n' now.  If you're interested <space>...




























(I don't know how to use the darn ^L yet)


Jodes (my wife's nickname) starts out like all other Valks cruising
through the Mines, picking up the experience and goodies.  Finding the
town altar belonging to Tyr, she has to wait awhile to do any serious
offering.  Little does she know that the next available altar (of ANY
diety) will not be seen until level 16 :-(

Along about dungeon level 10 she comes across a statue of a Barbarian.
"Cool," she smirks, quickly smashing Zenan (loser in a fight with a
cockatrice no doubt) open to find the +3 Mjollner and +3 GDSM - both
cursed, but who cares, eh?  With Odin obviously smiling on her, Jodes
feels that the quest is near...

Finally finding that altar on 16, she offers like crazy - LOVE those
cursed scrolls.  Soon she finds the Vorpal Blade at her feet - now she's
really in business!  After being promoted to Warrior, she sets out to meet
Norn, eat a bunch of giants (via blessed tinning kit), and lop Lord
Surtur's head off (wouldn't THAT be a cool quest artifact -- "Surtur's
eyes glow...What level do you want to teleport to?...).

Things fell in place - got levitation and conflict - making Luidos a piece
of cake.  Jodes takes the booty back to the town priest and picks up some
AC.  Unfortunately she will later really screw up by accidently offering a
Nurse (lying on the altar) giving these gains back, oh well.  Not all goes
perfectly though.  She errs in IDing a bag - you guessed it - BoH
implosion!  "OH SHIT," Jodes screams as dozens of wands, books, rings and
tools evaporate!  She will use EXTREME caution next time she tries to
protect her stuff with oilskin.

While building an inventory back up, Jodes (now a Heroine) stones Medusa
and takes on the Castle.  [She is now providing me a personal best!]  Here
she picks up a couple of great intrinsics including disintegration
resistance.  The WoW was a welcome sight as she  had terrible luck with
the lamps in the mine and quaffing fountains only managed to bring water
demons.  Anyway, speed boots and AoLS seemed the best bet at that time.
On to Gehennom...

Since this is her first visit to this part of the world, she takes her
time mapping all levels and getting into a LOT of close scrapes.  The only
consolation is that she has built herself up to about Exp 25 without doing
the bell trick :)  She discovers the watery level and dispenses with the
jabberwocks the clasic way (snicker-snack!), and locates the three Wiz
tower levels.  Being a first time traveler she gets frustrated and cannot
find her way in - sigh.  Also she is confused: how many towers?  how many
portals/doors/ladders? ...

She is a stubborn girl though, and spends a lotsa $ back at the Oracle
only to find out "easy things" like what to do with floating eyes and how
to find out if something is cursed!  Seems Jodes maxed out on the number
of oracles provided - no further donations are accepted.  Next, she (I)
begs at the ultimate altar -- r.g.h.  A couple of clues (THANKS) get her
back on track, and she goes up to meet Vlad.  He is quickly dispensed by a
flying Mjollnir, and Jodes picks up the prize.

Now more wandering around and searching.  Jodes the Champion figures out
how to get to the WoY but ... where the "hell" are the Book and the
Square?!?  She may be a rookie down here, but she knows better than to
grab the AoY before doing the necessary ceremony ;-)  Oh well, she
swallows her pride and goes back to the r.g.h. gang a second time.  This
time, no hints come back -- that must mean she is VERY CLOSE.  With
renewed spirit (and no other options) she keeps looking...thinking.
Finally a breakthrough (literally) and a fall down more levels (YES!).  At
the bottom she locates the vibration.  She heads back up with a theory on
the Book.

Now very aggressive, she gets to the Wiz's room  and thinks, "Alright, a
few krakens and I'm in there.  No problem, I'll put on my water boots and
I still have my AoLS on.  Let's do it!"

You guessed it: --The kraken grabs you...
                --The kraken pulls you into the moat...
                --Your amulet glows...
                --The kraken pulls you into the moat...
                --You drown...

What a time for the +5 Mjollnir to have a streak of misses!! :( :( :(
I guess she/I should have chosen the AoMB - sigh...
All of this with a wand of death in hand :(

Sad story huh?  I don't feel too bad though - great experience points
gained!!  Here are a few interesting notes:

* Died with 2,780,272 points (and a BIG pile of gems/$ on level 1)
* No abuses required: bell, polypile, savefiles 
* Never did find a magic lamp or another WoW
* Liches genocided (blessed scroll), after gremlins
* 3,394 creatures vanquished including:
	Yeenoghu, Jubilex, Croesus, Medusa
	Lord Surtur, Vlad the Impaler (of course)
	17 purple worms
	69 various adult dragons
* Had a pet Archon, turned nasty, which had to be locked in a room :)
* Saw SIX artifact weapons:
	Mjollnir     -|
	Vorpal Blade -| through offering
	Demonbane    -|
	Sunsword   -|
	Dragonbane -| by Archons
	Fire Brand -|

Well, that's about it.  Thanks for reading (& thanks for the hints).

Jodes (Jeff)

